{"parentUuid":"8582020f-987a-43c6-88b3-c57cfac895b5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"UserPromptSubmit","toolUseID":"b0f44ae0-ceba-4af4-ac4b-82c80a437ec9","hookEvent":"UserPromptSubmit","content":"<skill_relevance>\nRelevant to the current request: mattpocock-skills:research. Ignore this if it does not fit what the user actually asked for.\n</skill_relevance>","stdout":"<skill_relevance>\nRelevant to the current request: mattpocock-skills:research. Ignore this if it does not fit what the user actually asked for.\n</skill_relevance>\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"python3 \"$HOME/.claude/skill-router/router.py\"","durationMs":1107},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ed824317-d6ef-46a7-ba7f-5d1d321410a2","timestamp":"2026-10-07T15:51:01.863Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nUserPromptSubmit hook success: <skill_relevance>\nRelevant to the current request: mattpocock-skills:research. Ignore this if it does not fit what the user actually asked for.\n</skill_relevance>\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"4a9c3d55-7061-46f7-9760-4b5eacc869c5","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main"}
{"parentUuid":"ed824317-d6ef-46a7-ba7f-5d1d321410a2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"instructions","files":[{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md","type":"User","content":"# Machine\n\nMachine-specific shell, paths, and traps live in `~/.claude/machine.md` (gitignored; copy `machine.macos.md` or `machine.windows.md` to `machine.md` on a new machine). It is imported below.\n\n@machine.md\n\nTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive.\n\n**Session routine.** When working inside a project repo, follow the Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` and read `docs/STATUS.md` at the start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, and `git push` at the end. This is what keeps the two machines in step.\n\n# Workflow Expectations\n\n- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), finish with the produced file in hand. Check what exists first, then build the file even when a similar one already exists.\n- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n- Skills are tools: invoke one when it clearly fits the task.\n\n# Session Startup\n\nThe `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, a summary of `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot. Work from the injected copy.\n\n- If hook failures appear, surface them once on the first response, then continue. Entries mean a hook or scheduled job failed.\n- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response.\n- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand.\n- The injection is a frozen snapshot: mid-session writes take effect next session. Load anything further only when a question needs it.\n\n# Memory — routing only\n\nThe two-tier memory system (`~/.claude/global-memory/` and `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`) is owned by the **`memory-write` skill**, which holds the tier rules, character caps, slug rules, write steps, retrieval ladder, and daily-compiled-log rules.\n\nThe active project's Tier A memory (`~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`, indexed by its `MEMORY.md`) is **auto-injected by the harness** each session. Tier A files are also indexed by memsearch, so they stay recallable across projects.\n\n- Writing a fact — \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"save this\", \"forget about\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`\n- Recalling past context — \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`, retrieval-ladder section\n- Daily compiled logs at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/` are written only by `claude-memory-compiler`. Read one only when a question needs that day.\n- **Slugs differ per machine** (Mac `-Users-kristinarash-DEV-<X>`, Windows `C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-<X>`). Tier A written on one is not auto-injected on the other; memsearch still finds it. Durable project facts belong in the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n\n---\n\nMaintainer note: `AGENTS.md` diverges from this file on purpose (Codex has no Skill tool, so it spells out the memory rules). Keep them as separate files; the memory procedure's one home is the `memory-write` skill."},{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/machine.md","type":"User","content":"# Shell / Environment (macOS)\n\n- zsh/bash is the native surface on this machine. PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`, `/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) is installed only to run the KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs natively.\n- **The tool-path list has one home: `~/.claude/TOOLPATHS.md`.** Read that file when you need a path. Only the traps below are kept, because acting on them wrongly is expensive.\n- **Verify, don't trust any list.** `which -a <tool>` is authoritative. To read PATH honestly, scrub the environment first:\n  `env -i HOME=\"$HOME\" USER=\"$USER\" TERM=xterm SHELL=/bin/zsh /bin/zsh -lic 'echo $PATH'`\n- Traps:\n  - Python is PEP 668-managed. Use venvs or `uv`, never `pip install` globally.\n  - `uv` is a standalone install at `~/.local/bin/uv`, **not** Homebrew. Claude Code hooks call `$HOME/.local/bin/uv`; do not delete or relocate it.\n  - `timeout` is NOT installed (no GNU coreutils). Don't use it in scripts.\n  - Homebrew owns `/opt/homebrew/bin`. `/usr/local/bin` is empty and stays that way.\n  - Secrets live in the macOS Keychain, not in `~/.zshrc`.\n- DEV projects live at `~/DEV` (not `~/Desktop/DEV`). Workspace map: `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Primary storage drive (documents, data, deliverables): `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`."},{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"# ~/DEV — workspace map\n\nEric Rash — Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Sport science and\nfootball analytics, plus the agent system that runs them.\n\nThis file is a **map, not a rulebook**. Behavior rules live in\n`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Read only the index you need.\n\n## Areas\n\n| Area | Index | What lives there |\n|---|---|---|\n| Football | `FOOTBALL.md` | Game film, player analytics, CFB prediction. ~39k files — about two thirds of DEV. |\n| Performance | `PERFORMANCE.md` | Athlete monitoring, testing, load, risk. GPS, force plate, VALD, DEXA, S2. |\n| Research | `RESEARCH.md` | Literature, Zotero, book library, reading pipelines. |\n| Platform | `PLATFORM.md` | KeystoneOS, dashboards, CLIs, scheduled jobs. |\n| Program | `PROGRAM.md` | Staff reporting, curriculum, proposals, vetting, brand. |\n| Personal | `PERSONAL.md` | Side projects. Not Baylor work. |\n| Commands | `COMMANDS.md` | Desk reference: every report/project command Eric can run himself. |\n| Workflow | `WORKFLOW.md` | The ideal day, week and semester: which skill, mod and ritual, when and why. |\n\n## Elsewhere on disk\n\n`~/DEV` in this file means the workspace root: `~/DEV` on the Mac,\n`~/Desktop/DEV` on Windows. Paths that differ per machine are in `~/.claude/machine.md`.\n\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `~/DEV/_ARCHIVE/` | Parked projects. Not a git repo, so the consolidation sweep skips it. Has its own `README.md`. |\n| `~/DEV/_INBOX/` | Loose files from the `~/DEV` root. Own repo. |\n| SecondBrain vault | Obsidian vault, ~850 notes. Own `CLAUDE.md`. Mac `~/SecondBrain`, Windows `~/Desktop/SecondBrain`. |\n| `~/.claude/skills/` | ~45 skills (plugins add more) |\n| `~/go/bin/` | ~8 custom CLIs built with `cli-printing-press` |\n| `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/` | ~190 compiled articles |\n\n## Layout rules\n\nFull rules — grouping depth, the depth-2 discovery limit, and the gitignored-subtree\ntrap — live in project memory: `project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md`.\n\n- 23 projects carry their own `CLAUDE.md`. Read it before working in one.\n\n## Handling care\n\n- `DexaProject/` holds identifiable health data. It lives on Google Drive, not in\n  `~/DEV`, on **both** machines — one copy, reached by each machine's own path:\n  - Mac: `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/DexaProject`\n  - Windows: `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\DexaProject`\n\n  See `PERFORMANCE.md`.\n  Never paste its contents into chat, an artifact, or an external service.\n\n## Keeping this true\n\nWhen a file moves or a new project starts, **update the router in the same\nturn**. A stale pointer is worse than no pointer.\n\nThe counts above are approximate on purpose — they convey scale, not state, and\na `~` keeps ordinary growth from making this file wrong. Re-measure them only\nwhen one is off by enough to change a decision. Counts last checked 2026-10-02.\n\nMemory files named in these indexes (`project_*.md`, `user_*.md`) live in the\nworkspace's Tier A folder: Mac `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/`,\nWindows `~/.claude/projects/C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV/memory/`. They auto-load\nonly when cwd is the workspace root itself — from inside a sub-project, open them by path.\n\nSearch everything with `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`."},{"path":"/Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/MEMORY.md","type":"AutoMem","content":"# Memory Index\n\nOne line per memory: title, file, and a hook that says when to open it.\nNever put memory content here — the file itself holds the facts.\n\n- [Printing Press spec traps](project_printing-press-spec-traps.md) — writing a CLI spec\n- [zsh shell traps](project_zsh-shell-traps.md) — a zsh script misbehaves\n- [Status report sourcing](project_status-report-sourcing.md) — building the status report\n- [Fireflies CLI on Mac](project_fireflies-cli-broken-on-mac.md) — Fireflies CLI errors or renames\n- [gws Google Forms API](project_gws-forms-api.md) — creating or editing a Google Form\n- [Kenny Boyd doc review](project_kenny-boyd-doc-review-preferences.md) — writing a review doc for Kenny\n- [Kenny Boyd writing voice](project_kenny-boyd-writing-voice.md) — writing to, for, or like Kenny; SAS Leadership meeting\n- [Terminal Fluency workspace](project_terminal-fluency-workspace.md) — resuming Terminal Fluency\n- [PATH shadowing and cleanup](project_path-shadowing-and-cleanup.md) — PATH questions; before deleting any binary\n- [Backup/sync system](project_backup-sync-system.md) — backup routing or verification\n- [CFB Analytics Lab](project_cfb-analytics-lab.md) — resuming CFB Analytics Lab\n- [CFB forecast capture](project_cfb-forecast-capture.md) — weekly Big 12 forecast capture\n- [Drive FUSE rsync loop](project_drive-fuse-rsync-mtime-loop.md) — rsync keeps re-sending files to Drive, or hangs copying into Drive\n- [SecondBrain vault location](project_secondbrain-vault-location.md) — vault path questions\n- [Milvus lock misdiagnosis](project_milvus-lock-misdiagnosis.md) — Zotero/Milvus errors\n- [Memory compiler pipeline](project_memory-compiler-pipeline.md) — flush or daily-log problems\n- [memsearch index path drift](project_memsearch-index-path-drift.md) — memsearch indexes fewer paths\n- [memsearch hook timeout cap](project_memsearch-hook-timeout-cap.md) — memsearch slow or timing out\n- [Morning briefing retired](project_morning-briefing-retired.md) — old morning-briefing code or config\n- [graphify runtime setup](project_graphify-runtime-setup.md) — installing or rebuilding graphify\n- [graphify semantic extraction](project_graphify-semantic-extraction.md) — graphify quota or 429 errors\n- [Automation cadence](project_automation-cadence.md) — when a scheduled job or ritual runs\n- [S2 Cognition analysis](project_s2-cognition-analysis.md) — S2 Cognition work\n- [Sports teams](user_sports-teams.md) — an ambiguous WNBA ask\n- [Working-conditions bottleneck](user_working-conditions-bottleneck.md) — deciding whether to act unasked\n- [Zero-edit YouTube pipeline](reference_zero-edit-youtube-pipeline.md) — Claude Code video pipeline\n- [DEV layout and discovery](project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md) — moving or adding folders in ~/DEV\n- [KeystoneOS verification habits](project_keystoneos-verification-habits.md) — before asserting KeystoneOS state\n- [Portfolio registry provenance](project_portfolio-registry-write-provenance.md) — changing portfolio.json\n- [Command centre](project_command-centre.md) — retired 10-03 (board replaced it); localhost web-service security rules\n- [Vendored skill install](project_vendored-skill-install.md) — installing a vendored skill\n- [Vendored skill repair](project_vendored-skill-repair.md) — a skill returns empty output\n- [Personal site build routes](project_personal-site-build-routes.md) — building the personal site\n- [Book scan page ordering](project_book-scan-page-ordering.md) — scanned book pages out of order\n- [Ingest review gate](feedback_ingest-review-gate.md) — before ingest-book or other costly atomization\n- [Dormant threads](project_dormant-threads.md) — resuming Tezino CampPrep or FaceComps\n- [RTP CLA course](project_rtp-cla-course.md) — RTP CLA course work\n- [Post-merge cleanup](feedback_post-merge-cleanup.md) — after a merge; deleting worktrees or branches\n- [SCN sprint course](project_scn-sprint-course.md) — SCN sprint course work\n- [ATH Tech framework](project_ath-tech-framework.md) — ATH Tech framework work\n- [Supervisor log pipeline](project_supervisor-log-pipeline.md) — supervisor log or Kenny/Chris report\n- [dcg guard blocks](project_dcg-guard-blocks.md) — a Bash command was blocked\n- [Headless tool-deny gap](project_headless-claude-tool-deny-gap.md) — before calling a headless run read-only\n- [Config encoding damage from Windows](project_settings-json-bom-trap.md) — \"hook missing\" or garbled statusline\n- [Tech inventory refresh](project_tech-inventory-refresh.md) — refreshing the tech inventory\n- [Brain audit loop](project_brain-audit-loop.md) — scoring the second brain\n- [Hook two-copies trap](project_hook-two-copies-trap.md) — a hook patch \"reverts\"\n- [Child dental plan](user_child-dental-plan.md) — child dental care\n- [ELI5 output style](user_eli5-output-style.md) — output-style rules\n- [GitHub consolidation](project_github-consolidation.md) — ~/DEV repo layout or merge traps\n- [Skill bloat and promotion](project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md) — before touching ANY skill folder\n- [Prioritization slate](project_prioritization-slate.md) — Eric proposes a new project or idea\n- [Baylor department names](user_baylor-department-names.md) — writing staff-facing text\n- [Git Bash MSYS/AD stall](project_git-bash-msys-ad-stall.md) — Windows bash dies with `add_item errno 1`\n- [Backup task sleep-kill signature](project_backup-task-sleepkill-signature.md) — Windows backup exit 3221225786\n- [Sport-science thought partner](user_sport-science-thought-partner.md) — performance, S&C or rehab questions\n- [Third-party skill install](project_third-party-skill-install.md) — installing a third-party skill\n- [Admin docs house style](feedback_admin-docs-house-style.md) — building any doc for administration; Baylor_Doc_Style only, ask before breaking a page limit\n- [Box access via Box Drive](project_box-access-via-box-drive.md) — any Box request: Baylor blocks the MCP/connector, use the local Box Drive folder\n- [42Analytics YouTube pipeline](project_42analytics-youtube-pipeline.md) — YouTube channel to Flint; caption 429s, subagent summary.md block, empty Jev key\n- [Session hygiene](feedback_session-hygiene.md) — deleting sessions, \"where was I\", starting the day\n- [M365 agent access](project_m365-agent-access.md) — automating Teams, Outlook, Excel, Word or PowerPoint\n- [Harness time budget](feedback_harness-time-budget.md) — before any hook/skill/memory/system fix outside Friday's slot"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f1126773-af02-4598-b47a-599c8964ff65","timestamp":"2026-10-07T15:51:02.195Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/CLAUDE.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# Machine\n\nMachine-specific shell, paths, and traps live in `~/.claude/machine.md` (gitignored; copy `machine.macos.md` or `machine.windows.md` to `machine.md` on a new machine). It is imported below.\n\n@machine.md\n\nTwo machines share this setup: the MacBook (`~/DEV`) and the Baylor Windows laptop (`~/Desktop/DEV`). Projects sync through GitHub (`erash11`), documents through Google Drive.\n\n**Session routine.** When working inside a project repo, follow the Session routine in its `AGENTS.md`: `git pull` and read `docs/STATUS.md` at the start; update `STATUS.md`, commit, and `git push` at the end. This is what keeps the two machines in step.\n\n# Workflow Expectations\n\n- When asked to **create, merge, or consolidate an artifact** (calendar, deck, doc), finish with the produced file in hand. Check what exists first, then build the file even when a similar one already exists.\n- When the user types `/graphify`, invoke the Skill tool with `skill: \"graphify\"` before doing anything else.\n- Skills are tools: invoke one when it clearly fits the task.\n\n# Session Startup\n\nThe `keystone-unified-snapshot.js` SessionStart hook injects `global-memory/USER.md`, `global-memory/MEMORY.md`, a summary of `transcripts/.errors.log` (only when non-empty), and a pointer to the KeystoneOS snapshot. Work from the injected copy.\n\n- If hook failures appear, surface them once on the first response, then continue. Entries mean a hook or scheduled job failed.\n- If a **\"SessionStart hook could not read a required memory file\"** block appears, say so on the first response.\n- **If no `## User profile` block is in context at session start, the hook did not fire.** Say so, then read `USER.md`, `MEMORY.md` and `transcripts/.errors.log` by hand.\n- The injection is a frozen snapshot: mid-session writes take effect next session. Load anything further only when a question needs it.\n\n# Memory — routing only\n\nThe two-tier memory system (`~/.claude/global-memory/` and `~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`) is owned by the **`memory-write` skill**, which holds the tier rules, character caps, slug rules, write steps, retrieval ladder, and daily-compiled-log rules.\n\nThe active project's Tier A memory (`~/.claude/projects/<slug>/memory/`, indexed by its `MEMORY.md`) is **auto-injected by the harness** each session. Tier A files are also indexed by memsearch, so they stay recallable across projects.\n\n- Writing a fact — \"remember this\", \"note that\", \"save this\", \"forget about\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`\n- Recalling past context — \"did we already…?\", \"what did we decide about X\" → `Skill(\"memory-write\")`, retrieval-ladder section\n- Daily compiled logs at `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/daily/` are written only by `claude-memory-compiler`. Read one only when a question needs that day.\n- **Slugs differ per machine** (Mac `-Users-kristinarash-DEV-<X>`, Windows `C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV-<X>`). Tier A written on one is not auto-injected on the other; memsearch still finds it. Durable project facts belong in the repo's `docs/` so both machines see them.\n\n---\n\nMaintainer note: `AGENTS.md` diverges from this file on purpose (Codex has no Skill tool, so it spells out the memory rules). Keep them as separate files; the memory procedure's one home is the `memory-write` skill.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/machine.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# Shell / Environment (macOS)\n\n- zsh/bash is the native surface on this machine. PowerShell 7 (`pwsh`, `/opt/homebrew/bin/pwsh`) is installed only to run the KeystoneOS `.ps1` jobs natively.\n- **The tool-path list has one home: `~/.claude/TOOLPATHS.md`.** Read that file when you need a path. Only the traps below are kept, because acting on them wrongly is expensive.\n- **Verify, don't trust any list.** `which -a <tool>` is authoritative. To read PATH honestly, scrub the environment first:\n  `env -i HOME=\"$HOME\" USER=\"$USER\" TERM=xterm SHELL=/bin/zsh /bin/zsh -lic 'echo $PATH'`\n- Traps:\n  - Python is PEP 668-managed. Use venvs or `uv`, never `pip install` globally.\n  - `uv` is a standalone install at `~/.local/bin/uv`, **not** Homebrew. Claude Code hooks call `$HOME/.local/bin/uv`; do not delete or relocate it.\n  - `timeout` is NOT installed (no GNU coreutils). Don't use it in scripts.\n  - Homebrew owns `/opt/homebrew/bin`. `/usr/local/bin` is empty and stays that way.\n  - Secrets live in the macOS Keychain, not in `~/.zshrc`.\n- DEV projects live at `~/DEV` (not `~/Desktop/DEV`). Workspace map: `~/DEV/CLAUDE.md`.\n- Primary storage drive (documents, data, deliverables): `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive`.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/DEV/CLAUDE.md (project instructions, checked into the codebase):\n\n# ~/DEV — workspace map\n\nEric Rash — Applied Performance, Baylor Athletics. Sport science and\nfootball analytics, plus the agent system that runs them.\n\nThis file is a **map, not a rulebook**. Behavior rules live in\n`~/.claude/CLAUDE.md`. Read only the index you need.\n\n## Areas\n\n| Area | Index | What lives there |\n|---|---|---|\n| Football | `FOOTBALL.md` | Game film, player analytics, CFB prediction. ~39k files — about two thirds of DEV. |\n| Performance | `PERFORMANCE.md` | Athlete monitoring, testing, load, risk. GPS, force plate, VALD, DEXA, S2. |\n| Research | `RESEARCH.md` | Literature, Zotero, book library, reading pipelines. |\n| Platform | `PLATFORM.md` | KeystoneOS, dashboards, CLIs, scheduled jobs. |\n| Program | `PROGRAM.md` | Staff reporting, curriculum, proposals, vetting, brand. |\n| Personal | `PERSONAL.md` | Side projects. Not Baylor work. |\n| Commands | `COMMANDS.md` | Desk reference: every report/project command Eric can run himself. |\n| Workflow | `WORKFLOW.md` | The ideal day, week and semester: which skill, mod and ritual, when and why. |\n\n## Elsewhere on disk\n\n`~/DEV` in this file means the workspace root: `~/DEV` on the Mac,\n`~/Desktop/DEV` on Windows. Paths that differ per machine are in `~/.claude/machine.md`.\n\n| Path | What it is |\n|---|---|\n| `~/DEV/_ARCHIVE/` | Parked projects. Not a git repo, so the consolidation sweep skips it. Has its own `README.md`. |\n| `~/DEV/_INBOX/` | Loose files from the `~/DEV` root. Own repo. |\n| SecondBrain vault | Obsidian vault, ~850 notes. Own `CLAUDE.md`. Mac `~/SecondBrain`, Windows `~/Desktop/SecondBrain`. |\n| `~/.claude/skills/` | ~45 skills (plugins add more) |\n| `~/go/bin/` | ~8 custom CLIs built with `cli-printing-press` |\n| `~/.claude/claude-memory-compiler/knowledge/` | ~190 compiled articles |\n\n## Layout rules\n\nFull rules — grouping depth, the depth-2 discovery limit, and the gitignored-subtree\ntrap — live in project memory: `project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md`.\n\n- 23 projects carry their own `CLAUDE.md`. Read it before working in one.\n\n## Handling care\n\n- `DexaProject/` holds identifiable health data. It lives on Google Drive, not in\n  `~/DEV`, on **both** machines — one copy, reached by each machine's own path:\n  - Mac: `~/Library/CloudStorage/GoogleDrive-eric.rash11@gmail.com/My Drive/00_Primary_Storage_Drive/DexaProject`\n  - Windows: `G:\\My Drive\\00_Primary_Storage_Drive\\DexaProject`\n\n  See `PERFORMANCE.md`.\n  Never paste its contents into chat, an artifact, or an external service.\n\n## Keeping this true\n\nWhen a file moves or a new project starts, **update the router in the same\nturn**. A stale pointer is worse than no pointer.\n\nThe counts above are approximate on purpose — they convey scale, not state, and\na `~` keeps ordinary growth from making this file wrong. Re-measure them only\nwhen one is off by enough to change a decision. Counts last checked 2026-10-02.\n\nMemory files named in these indexes (`project_*.md`, `user_*.md`) live in the\nworkspace's Tier A folder: Mac `~/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/`,\nWindows `~/.claude/projects/C--Users-eric-rash-Desktop-DEV/memory/`. They auto-load\nonly when cwd is the workspace root itself — from inside a sub-project, open them by path.\n\nSearch everything with `memsearch search \"<query>\" --top-k 5`.\n\nContents of /Users/kristinarash/.claude/projects/-Users-kristinarash-DEV/memory/MEMORY.md (user's auto-memory, persists across conversations):\n\n# Memory Index\n\nOne line per memory: title, file, and a hook that says when to open it.\nNever put memory content here — the file itself holds the facts.\n\n- [Printing Press spec traps](project_printing-press-spec-traps.md) — writing a CLI spec\n- [zsh shell traps](project_zsh-shell-traps.md) — a zsh script misbehaves\n- [Status report sourcing](project_status-report-sourcing.md) — building the status report\n- [Fireflies CLI on Mac](project_fireflies-cli-broken-on-mac.md) — Fireflies CLI errors or renames\n- [gws Google Forms API](project_gws-forms-api.md) — creating or editing a Google Form\n- [Kenny Boyd doc review](project_kenny-boyd-doc-review-preferences.md) — writing a review doc for Kenny\n- [Kenny Boyd writing voice](project_kenny-boyd-writing-voice.md) — writing to, for, or like Kenny; SAS Leadership meeting\n- [Terminal Fluency workspace](project_terminal-fluency-workspace.md) — resuming Terminal Fluency\n- [PATH shadowing and cleanup](project_path-shadowing-and-cleanup.md) — PATH questions; before deleting any binary\n- [Backup/sync system](project_backup-sync-system.md) — backup routing or verification\n- [CFB Analytics Lab](project_cfb-analytics-lab.md) — resuming CFB Analytics Lab\n- [CFB forecast capture](project_cfb-forecast-capture.md) — weekly Big 12 forecast capture\n- [Drive FUSE rsync loop](project_drive-fuse-rsync-mtime-loop.md) — rsync keeps re-sending files to Drive, or hangs copying into Drive\n- [SecondBrain vault location](project_secondbrain-vault-location.md) — vault path questions\n- [Milvus lock misdiagnosis](project_milvus-lock-misdiagnosis.md) — Zotero/Milvus errors\n- [Memory compiler pipeline](project_memory-compiler-pipeline.md) — flush or daily-log problems\n- [memsearch index path drift](project_memsearch-index-path-drift.md) — memsearch indexes fewer paths\n- [memsearch hook timeout cap](project_memsearch-hook-timeout-cap.md) — memsearch slow or timing out\n- [Morning briefing retired](project_morning-briefing-retired.md) — old morning-briefing code or config\n- [graphify runtime setup](project_graphify-runtime-setup.md) — installing or rebuilding graphify\n- [graphify semantic extraction](project_graphify-semantic-extraction.md) — graphify quota or 429 errors\n- [Automation cadence](project_automation-cadence.md) — when a scheduled job or ritual runs\n- [S2 Cognition analysis](project_s2-cognition-analysis.md) — S2 Cognition work\n- [Sports teams](user_sports-teams.md) — an ambiguous WNBA ask\n- [Working-conditions bottleneck](user_working-conditions-bottleneck.md) — deciding whether to act unasked\n- [Zero-edit YouTube pipeline](reference_zero-edit-youtube-pipeline.md) — Claude Code video pipeline\n- [DEV layout and discovery](project_dev-layout-and-discovery.md) — moving or adding folders in ~/DEV\n- [KeystoneOS verification habits](project_keystoneos-verification-habits.md) — before asserting KeystoneOS state\n- [Portfolio registry provenance](project_portfolio-registry-write-provenance.md) — changing portfolio.json\n- [Command centre](project_command-centre.md) — retired 10-03 (board replaced it); localhost web-service security rules\n- [Vendored skill install](project_vendored-skill-install.md) — installing a vendored skill\n- [Vendored skill repair](project_vendored-skill-repair.md) — a skill returns empty output\n- [Personal site build routes](project_personal-site-build-routes.md) — building the personal site\n- [Book scan page ordering](project_book-scan-page-ordering.md) — scanned book pages out of order\n- [Ingest review gate](feedback_ingest-review-gate.md) — before ingest-book or other costly atomization\n- [Dormant threads](project_dormant-threads.md) — resuming Tezino CampPrep or FaceComps\n- [RTP CLA course](project_rtp-cla-course.md) — RTP CLA course work\n- [Post-merge cleanup](feedback_post-merge-cleanup.md) — after a merge; deleting worktrees or branches\n- [SCN sprint course](project_scn-sprint-course.md) — SCN sprint course work\n- [ATH Tech framework](project_ath-tech-framework.md) — ATH Tech framework work\n- [Supervisor log pipeline](project_supervisor-log-pipeline.md) — supervisor log or Kenny/Chris report\n- [dcg guard blocks](project_dcg-guard-blocks.md) — a Bash command was blocked\n- [Headless tool-deny gap](project_headless-claude-tool-deny-gap.md) — before calling a headless run read-only\n- [Config encoding damage from Windows](project_settings-json-bom-trap.md) — \"hook missing\" or garbled statusline\n- [Tech inventory refresh](project_tech-inventory-refresh.md) — refreshing the tech inventory\n- [Brain audit loop](project_brain-audit-loop.md) — scoring the second brain\n- [Hook two-copies trap](project_hook-two-copies-trap.md) — a hook patch \"reverts\"\n- [Child dental plan](user_child-dental-plan.md) — child dental care\n- [ELI5 output style](user_eli5-output-style.md) — output-style rules\n- [GitHub consolidation](project_github-consolidation.md) — ~/DEV repo layout or merge traps\n- [Skill bloat and promotion](project_skill-bloat-and-promotion.md) — before touching ANY skill folder\n- [Prioritization slate](project_prioritization-slate.md) — Eric proposes a new project or idea\n- [Baylor department names](user_baylor-department-names.md) — writing staff-facing text\n- [Git Bash MSYS/AD stall](project_git-bash-msys-ad-stall.md) — Windows bash dies with `add_item errno 1`\n- [Backup task sleep-kill signature](project_backup-task-sleepkill-signature.md) — Windows backup exit 3221225786\n- [Sport-science thought partner](user_sport-science-thought-partner.md) — performance, S&C or rehab questions\n- [Third-party skill install](project_third-party-skill-install.md) — installing a third-party skill\n- [Admin docs house style](feedback_admin-docs-house-style.md) — building any doc for administration; Baylor_Doc_Style only, ask before breaking a page limit\n- [Box access via Box Drive](project_box-access-via-box-drive.md) — any Box request: Baylor blocks the MCP/connector, use the local Box Drive folder\n- [42Analytics YouTube pipeline](project_42analytics-youtube-pipeline.md) — YouTube channel to Flint; caption 429s, subagent summary.md block, empty Jev key\n- [Session hygiene](feedback_session-hygiene.md) — deleting sessions, \"where was I\", starting the day\n- [M365 agent access](project_m365-agent-access.md) — automating Teams, Outlook, Excel, Word or PowerPoint\n- [Harness time budget](feedback_harness-time-budget.md) — before any hook/skill/memory/system fix outside Friday's slot\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"user","session_id":"4a9c3d55-7061-46f7-9760-4b5eacc869c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"4a9c3d55-7061-46f7-9760-4b5eacc869c5","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main"}
