{"parentUuid":"811791d4-f048-4d09-b649-ed34785f59ef","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d3b1653a-ee1e-44c9-819a-56d6df28281a","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CK8JkZpyUytRXgbLX7r4CN","type":"tool_result","content":"closeout off\ndev-sync off\nfive-slides-generator off\nnew-project off\nwatch off\nlast30days off\narticulation-skill off\n## library-advisor\ndescription: >-\n  Consult a grounded domain advisor built from the curated book library; answers only\n  from ingested entries and cites every claim. Use when the user says \"ask my <domain>\n  advisor\", \"/library-advisor <domain> <question>\", \"what would my library say about…\",\n## library-review\ndescription: >-\n  Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and\n  propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says\n  \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain>\n## startup\ndescription: >-\n  Start of day, or sitting down at either machine: sync this machine against GitHub,\n  then report where the last session left off and wait. Use when Eric says '/startup',\n  'good morning', 'starting up', 'where did I leave off', 'what was I working on',\n## synced/507a61e7-48f7-48f7-8c5b-df28be667fa3_416bef0f-da27-46f8-9a3c-18dedd0186a1/morning\ndescription: \"Render the user's morning brief as a styled HTML artifact, or set it up as a recurring weekday task. Use only when the user explicitly asks to run, see, or set up their morning brief, or if they invoke /morning by name. A question about their day, schedule, or calendar is not by itself\n---\n\n## Context\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cd941d16-ece0-45f7-a4a4-472169c8fbe3","timestamp":"2026-10-07T15:53:51.502Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"closeout off\ndev-sync off\nfive-slides-generator off\nnew-project off\nwatch off\nlast30days off\narticulation-skill off\n## library-advisor\ndescription: >-\n  Consult a grounded domain advisor built from the curated book library; answers only\n  from ingested entries and cites every claim. Use when the user says \"ask my <domain>\n  advisor\", \"/library-advisor <domain> <question>\", \"what would my library say about…\",\n## library-review\ndescription: >-\n  Review a book-library domain for gaps, contested entries, and missing coverage, and\n  propose new entries. Manual loop — proposes, you approve. Use when the user says\n  \"review my library\", \"/library-review <domain>\", \"what's missing from my <domain>\n## startup\ndescription: >-\n  Start of day, or sitting down at either machine: sync this machine against GitHub,\n  then report where the last session left off and wait. Use when Eric says '/startup',\n  'good morning', 'starting up', 'where did I leave off', 'what was I working on',\n## synced/507a61e7-48f7-48f7-8c5b-df28be667fa3_416bef0f-da27-46f8-9a3c-18dedd0186a1/morning\ndescription: \"Render the user's morning brief as a styled HTML artifact, or set it up as a recurring weekday task. Use only when the user explicitly asks to run, see, or set up their morning brief, or if they invoke /morning by name. A question about their day, schedule, or calendar is not by itself\n---\n\n## Context","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/kristinarash/DEV","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"811791d4-f048-4d09-b649-ed34785f59ef","session_id":"4a9c3d55-7061-46f7-9760-4b5eacc869c5","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/kristinarash/DEV","sessionId":"4a9c3d55-7061-46f7-9760-4b5eacc869c5","version":"2.1.292","gitBranch":"main"}
